{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/585592-beast-henderson-and-knight-help-request-for-making-them-from-concept-to-reality","id":585592,"title":"[Beast] Henderson and Knight. Help request for making them from concept to reality.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-09T20:53:39-07:00","id":585592,"title":"[Beast] Henderson and Knight. Help request for making them from concept to reality.","content":"Allow me to introduce my Noble Dark NPC duo. James Henderson and Nickolas Knight. Or Henderson and Knight for short. I need a bit of help refining them and developing there sheets so bare with me. There theme is Noble Dark. These individuals are not Bright and Sunny, one is a lurking monstrosity, the other is the princess kidnapping dragon. I'll be asking a series of questions to help work a sheet up on these NPC's. My knowledge of WoD mechanics is rather shaky at best, but i find I like beasts quite a bit. Our PC's are going for a sort of Nobel dark model, with our mixed group of Uratha and Kindred.<br /> <br /> James Henderson: Lurker Nemisis. SVU Detective by trade Henderson feeds on those who abuse there loved ones. He's usually the first on on the location for a 273D. His personality is a mix between Sam Burke (IIRC) from Spawn and the spin off Sam and Twitch, and Elliot Stabler of Law and Order SVU.<br /> <br /> His partner Knight is a Raptor Collector, who collects the Victims, taking them to his lair. He then works on the victim to break them out of the Victim psychology. He is a handsome man, charming, charismatic man.<br /> <br /> SO here are a few conceptual questions, let's say Henderson and Knight respond to a 273D (Domestic Violence) and Henderson arrests the abuser (Perhaps smacking there head against the door of the car &quot;on accident&quot;, repeatedly Feeding once. Knight leads away the victim and takes that person to his Lair. Some time later the abuser is in court Henderson testifies and forces the man to face justice feeding again. Does Knight get to feed again when this person is brought face to face with there former Victim who no longer acts and behaves like there property, showing the connection is broken?<br /> Also can night bring the victims into his Lair to live for a time while he works on there minds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T01:59:15-07:00","id":585774,"title":"","content":"I'd say that Henderson can feed as often as he likes from the same person as long as it's a different punishment- beating, ruined reputation, public humiliation, incarceration, seizure of property, it's all good, depending on his satiety level. <br /> <br /> As for Knight, collecting is about the acquisition, once the victims aren't victims anymore, they wouldn't be part of his collection anymore. Unless you changed it so that he collects ex-victims, his metaphorically taking the power away from their attackers making them his, then he could feed after breaking the connection.<br /> <br /> If the attacker tried to victimize them again, and Knight was able to snatch victory from their grasp, I could see another feeding roll, but I could also see the argument against it. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 07-10-2015, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:05:04-07:00","id":586083,"title":"","content":"Okay. That is interesting, so nemesis have an easier time feeding as cops. What I had thought is that when the person stops being a victim they would be leaving there victimology behind them, thus creating something a painting, sculpture, crystal ball holding that part of them that they are leaving, behind thus his hoard would look something like the prophecy room from Harry Potter or an art gallery. I will have to keep that in mind. But it is possible.<br /> <br /> I figured rubbing someone's face in the fact that you took away something of theirs would allow a hoarder to feed again from the same collected item. Guess I was wrong there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}